    <bpmn:process id="W_W3389" name="W3389. Cash-Availability-Aware Discount Throttling &amp; Treasury Authorization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily cash-position review (links to VS-18.1); liquidity event
Frequency: Daily + event-driven
Volume: Full dynamic-discounting portfolio
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: Treasury Manager, AP Manager, CFO
Source: workflow W3389 — Cash-Availability-Aware Discount Throttling &amp; Treasury Authorization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3389_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3389_Lane1" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3389_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3389_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3389_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3389_Lane2" name="AP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3389_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3389_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3389_Start4" name="Daily cash-position review (links to VS-18.1); liquidity event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3389_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3389_Task5" name="Treasury review the daily cash position and short-term forecast (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Treasury review the daily cash position and short-term forecast (links to VS-18.1/W233): operating balance, sweep availability (W323), capex draw needs (links to VS-40), tax/statutory outflows (links to VS-79), and import/LC settlements (links to VS-02.2); compute the early-payment funding envelope
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3389_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3389_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3389_Task6" name="Treasury set/adjust the daily early-payment throttle (cap, vendor-tier…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Treasury set/adjust the daily early-payment throttle (cap, vendor-tier, curve-band) based on cash availability; throttle down in tight-liquidity periods (e.g., pre-VAT/statutory remittance, import-LC week) and up in surplus periods
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3389_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3389_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3389_Task7" name="AP execute within the throttle, escalate over-throttle high-value acceptances…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AP execute within the throttle, escalate over-throttle high-value acceptances to Treasury/CFO for ad-hoc authorization (links to W3390), and report throttling impact on yield capture to the weekly review (W3388)
Responsible (R): AP Manager / Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3389_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3389_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3389_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3389_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-545 (ensure controlled execution — Dynamic Discounting &amp; Early-Payment Operations (PA-105.2).) | - operational: daily throttle tied to forecast; operational: dynamic, forecast-aware throttling
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
