    <bpmn:process id="W_W3390" name="W3390. Vendor-Initiated Early-Payment Request &amp; Ad-Hoc Discount Approval" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor early-payment request via portal (links to VS-03.4)
Frequency: Exception-driven
Volume: ~10–30 ad-hoc requests/month
Owner: AP Manager
Participants: AP Manager, Treasury Manager, Vendor, Procurement
Source: workflow W3390 — Vendor-Initiated Early-Payment Request &amp; Ad-Hoc Discount Approval</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3390_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3390_Lane1" name="Vendor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3390_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3390_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3390_Lane2" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3390_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3390_Lane3" name="AP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3390_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3390_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3390_Start5" name="Vendor early-payment request via portal (links to VS-03.4)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3390_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3390_Task6" name="Vendor raises an ad-hoc early-payment request via the supplier portal outside…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor raises an ad-hoc early-payment request via the supplier portal outside the auto-offer curve (e.g., distress, working-capital need); AP/Treasury receive the request with invoice, amount, requested date, and proposed discount
Responsible (R): Vendor / AP Manager
Accountable (A): AP Manager
Duration: Per request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3390_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3390_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3390_Task7" name="Treasury/Procurement assess the request: vendor health/strategic importance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Treasury/Procurement assess the request: vendor health/strategic importance (links to VS-67), discount vs curve/yield (W3388), cash availability (W3389), and any distress signal warranting escalation (links to VS-68 trade-credit-risk methodology); approve, counter, or decline within SLA
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Procurement
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: Per request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3390_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3390_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3390_Task8" name="AP execute the approved ad-hoc early payment, post the agreed discount (W3392)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AP execute the approved ad-hoc early payment, post the agreed discount (W3392), and log the request outcome for governance (W3384); feed repeat ad-hoc patterns into curve/enrollment review (W3385)
Responsible (R): AP Manager
Accountable (A): AP Manager
Duration: Per request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3390_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3390_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3390_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
